---
// Problem.astro — Problem framing section using PAS framework.
// Three pain-point cards targeting professionals, students, and developers.
// Each card has an icon, heading, and outcome-focused description.
// Uses existing .problem-grid and .pain CSS classes from global.css.
---

<section class="section" id="problem">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head center reveal">
      <span class="h-kicker center">The Problem</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">Your voice deserves better tools.</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">
        Today&rsquo;s dictation tools force you to choose between privacy and
        convenience &mdash; and none of them solve the full picture. Professionals,
        students, and developers all hit the same wall: slow typing, scattered notes,
        and tools that send your voice to the cloud.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="problem-grid">
      <!-- ========== PROFESSIONALS ========== -->
      <article class="card sheen lift pad pain reveal">
        <div class="pain-ic">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <rect x="2" y="3" width="20" height="14" rx="2"/>
            <path d="M8 21h8"/>
            <path d="M12 17v4"/>
            <path d="M8 7h.01M12 7h.01M16 7h.01"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Meeting note fatigue</h3>
        <p>
          Back-to-back meetings leave you with a dozen half-typed summaries.
          By the time you finish writing up one call, the next one has started.
          Hours lost every week just typing out what was said.
        </p>
      </article>

      <!-- ========== STUDENTS ========== -->
      <article class="card sheen lift pad pain reveal d1">
        <div class="pain-ic">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M4 19.5A2.5 2.5 0 016.5 17H20"/>
            <path d="M6.5 2H20v20H6.5A2.5 2.5 0 014 19.5v-15A2.5 2.5 0 016.5 2z"/>
            <path d="M8 7h6M8 11h8"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Scattered lecture notes</h3>
        <p>
          Lectures move fast. You&rsquo;re either typing frantically or missing
          key insights. By the end of the day, your notes live across three
          different apps &mdash; and you can never find the one you need.
        </p>
      </article>

      <!-- ========== DEVELOPERS ========== -->
      <article class="card sheen lift pad pain reveal d2">
        <div class="pain-ic">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M12 3l7 3v5c0 4.5-3 7.6-7 9-4-1.4-7-4.5-7-9V6l7-3z"/>
            <path d="M9 12h.01M15 12h.01"/>
            <path d="M9 12a3.5 3.5 0 006 0"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Cloud privacy risk</h3>
        <p>
          Most voice tools upload your audio to someone else&rsquo;s server
          before giving you text back. You can&rsquo;t use them for client calls,
          confidential standups, or anything you care about keeping private.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
